cellPad: keyboard right stick, L3/R3 and arrows-as-stick mode; PAD_FILE can hold the sticks.

A first-person game cannot be played from the keyboard without a camera: the keyboard fallback left the right stick
centred and had no L3/R3. I/J/K/L now drive the right stick and C/V press L3/R3. The arrows still press the d-pad and
push the left stick; PAD_ARROWS_STICK_ONLY=1 makes them the left stick alone and moves the d-pad to T/F/G/H, for
titles where the d-pad has its own actions (Resistance 3 switches weapons and gadgets on it).

PAD_FILE accepts four optional stick values after the poll count ("mask polls lx ly rx ry", 0-255, 128 centred), held
for those polls, so scripted runs can walk and turn.

Upstream: not proposed yet.

---

